<title>USA: Ride sees Q4 loss $0.20-$0.22/shr.</title>
<headline>Ride sees Q4 loss $0.20-$0.22/shr.</headline>
<dateline>PRESTON, Wash. 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ride Inc said Monday it would take $9 million in restructuring and write-down charges in the fourth quarter and expects to post a loss of $2.2-$2.4 million, or $0.20-$0.22 per share, for the period.</p>
<p>A year earlier it reported a net profit of $1.87 million, or $0.16 per share.</p>
<p>Sales for the fourth quarter are expected to be between $13 million and $15 million, versus $25.7 million a year eartlier, it said.</p>
</text>
